<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Nightingale returns two weeks after her first visit to review her tests, and saw the infectious diseases physician this morning. She has kept the activity and symptom diary we agreed on. It shows the pattern she described: on days she works more than about three hours or goes out, she feels worse the next day or the day after, with aches as if she had the flu, heavier fatigue, and poor concentration that take two to four days to settle. She sleeps nine hours but wakes unrefreshed. Standing at the stove or in a line still makes her lightheaded with a pounding heart within a few minutes. She has started drinking more fluid, about 1.8 L a day. She takes acetaminophen two or three times a week for muscle aches and headache. Her mood is frustrated but not low, and she has no thoughts of self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>No change; diary confirms delayed post-exertional malaise lasting two to four days</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Nine hours, unrefreshing</td></tr><tr><td>Orthostatic symptoms</td><td>Lightheaded with palpitations within minutes of standing</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>Muscle aches and headache; acetaminophen two or three times a week</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Working about three hours a day, reclined</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Frustrated, not depressed; no thoughts of self-harm</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Positive</td><td>Fatigue worsened by activity; no fever, night sweats, or weight loss</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Positive</td><td>Palpitations and lightheadedness on standing; no chest pain or syncope</td></tr><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Positive</td><td>Diffuse muscle aches; no localized back, hip, or joint pain or swelling</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Positive</td><td>Poor concentration and word-finding after exertion; headaches; no weakness or numbness</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Negative</td><td>No low mood, anhedonia, or thoughts of self-harm</td></tr><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Negative</td><td>No diarrhea, abdominal pain, or bleeding</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>6 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

